# Which reader reads the files of @term/mill (call/code/role-of.ts reads this file: a manifest `role` line, else
# base/role.tree, else role.tree here).
#
# Every `.tree` under code/ DEFINES a dialect: `code/<dialect>/base.tree` names it (`mill fork` / `bind mine, load
# ./mine`), and its `mine.tree` and `mint.tree` hold the rules the toolchain reads with readMineGrammar and
# readMintGrammar (deck/make/code/compile/mill-load.ts). None of them is a program. Without this file every one was
# milled as Term code, so each `mine` rule read as a call to an undefined task and the editor showed over a
# thousand errors on one open grammar file.
#
# The `mill` role is read by deck/make/code/compile/mill-check.ts: the file parses, every `load` resolves, every
# `find` names something its target declares, and every `mint <x>, like <form>` names a form a load brings in.
# test/compile/mill-grammar.ts holds all 344 files to the same function.

role mill
  take @/code/**/*.tree
